# Replay demo on a REAL bus — vcan0, CAN-FD capable.
#
# The other replay demo (replay-demo.blobnet) plays a .log onto an in-process bus and needs no
# drivers at all; this one puts the same kind of traffic on a real SocketCAN interface, which is
# what a bench looks like. Bring the interface up first:
#
#   ./scripts/setup_wsl_kernel.sh      # loads vcan, creates vcan0/vcan1 at mtu 72 (CAN-FD)
#
# Press ▶ Start and the recording plays onto vcan0. The frames are OURS, so the trace counts
# them as TX-S and claims their echoes; `candump -x vcan0` shows the same frames on the wire.
#
# This is PLAYBACK, not simulation: the alive counters and CRCs are whatever the recording holds.
# They are consistent within a lap and jump backwards at a `loop:` wrap. Simulated nodes stamp
# those fresh (see `protect:` in docs/simulation.md); a recording cannot.
#
# For a real vehicle capture, add the two facts a recording cannot supply:
#   bus: CAN1                 # WHICH recorded bus feeds this channel (a .mf4 holds several)
#   exclude: [VCM_C]          # the ECU under test — so it stays the only source of its frames
project:
  name: Replay onto vcan0
channels:
  - name: CAN1
    type: can
    interface: vcan0
    mode: replay
    databases:
      - dbc/blobly_net.dbc
    replay:
      source: samples/demo.mf4
      speed: 1.0
      loop: false
